NAME
    stdin - the files named, else the console, for the /BIN filters
            (#include "../lib_stdin.c")

SYNOPSIS
    #include "../lib_stdin.c"     (includes lib_globx.c and lib_fs.c)
    if (openarg(argstr()) == 2) { notfound("cmd"); return; }
    while ((c = nextc()) != 65535) ...

DESCRIPTION
    The input side of cat, wc, head, tail, more, sort, uniq, sed, awk
    and grep.

    openarg(tail)  0 = no file named (the console), 1 = ready, 2 = a
                   name was not found (gbad points at it). Every word
                   of tail is a file, a glob (expanded by globx), or
                   "-" for the console, read one after the other as ONE
                   stream. All the names are checked before anything is
                   read.
    nextc()        the next byte of that stream, 65535 at its end. The
                   console is conin(): no echo, Ctrl-D ends it.
    notfound(cmd)  prints "cmd: not found: WORD" after a 2.

    Globals:
        sepfiles   set it to 1 before the first nextc() to end every
                   file with a line feed (a line tool must not glue the
                   last line of one file to the first of the next);
                   leave it 0 for the byte-exact tools (cat, wc)
        curname    the name being read ("-" for the console): grep's
                   "NAME:" prefix
        gnf        how many names openarg found
        gfiles     the names, GSLOT (64) bytes each

LIMITS
    GMAX (24) names in all, after glob expansion; more are dropped.
    One read handle is open at a time (opened as the stream reaches the
    file, closed at its end).

NOTES
    Changed from the P8X version: every word of the tail, not just the
    first; "-" for the console; sepfiles and curname; Y1/OS fopen and
    fgetc (relative names resolve in the OS, so RDBUF, FRESOLVE, the
    absolute-path building and the carry tests are gone); the console
    is conin() with 65535 at Ctrl-D, where the P8X read getchar(),
    which could be a < redirect (Y1/OS has no redirection yet).
    Ported from P8X os/commands/lib_stdin.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    rdline, globx, glob, cat, grep, sort, wc
